invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_public returns without wiping its running power. In
  the signer's check that power ends as the encoded message when the
  check passes, and as a value that with the message factors the modulus
  when it fails. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below one
  signature and finds two words of the encoded message there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(x, sizeof x);
    ct_wipe(acc, sizeof acc);
--- new
    ct_wipe(x, sizeof x);
